The proposed solution will integrate with existing practices and not constitute a rupture in the agents' modes of work. It will provide contextualized answers to the agents' demands, facilitate access to information, improve answer quality, reduce processing times, and assist in drafting letters or answers to users. The tool will also accompany the agents in instructing files, such as town planning, social aids, and civil status, and suggest actions or steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process.

Our technical architecture will leverage expertise in AI/ML systems, cloud architecture, API integration, data engineering, and cybersecurity. We will utilize APIs like REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, and API gateways such as Kong and Apigee, to integrate with existing systems of information, business softwares, electronic management of documents, and user directories.

To ensure high availability (99.9%) and fast response times (within 2 seconds), we will design a cloud-based architecture using providers like OVHcloud, Scaleway, or Outscale (SecNumCloud). We will employ containerization using Docker and orchestration with Kubernetes (K8s) to ensure scalability and reliability.

Our solution will guarantee data sovereignty and security by hosting the data exclusively within the European Union, protected appropriately using encryption and anonymization if necessary. We will also utilize our experience in security design patterns such as zero-trust network architecture, VLAN segmentation, and mTLS between services.

We are committed to protecting sensitive data through encryption and anonymization techniques. Our GDPR posture includes the use of anonymisation tools like Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, ensuring personal data protection. We maintain a RAID log, Decision log, and Change request process, as well as establish a Steering committee that meets on a monthly basis to review progress.

Our AI solution will utilize large language models (LLMs) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to assist agents in their daily missions. Our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, can be fine-tuned on the client's dataset to provide accurate and relevant responses. We have experience with explainability methods like source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME.

We prioritize environmental sustainability and will propose a solution that relies as much as possible on infrastructures with low carbon impact. Our green hosting partners program includes OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France and using 100% renewable energy. By hosting the city's systems on these infrastructures, we can significantly reduce the environmental footprint associated with their information systems.

Our budget proposal takes into account the global budget allocated to the project (3 million euros over a duration of 4 years) and our target gross margin percentage (28%). We will optimize costs while ensuring quality of service through process improvements, efficient resource allocation, and potential renegotiation of rates with subcontractors. Our pricing model includes infrastructure margin, software license resale margin, and target gross margin.

We believe that our proposed solution meets the City of Belval's requirements for improving efficiency, reducing environmental footprint, and providing a high level of availability and security. We are committed to delivering an intelligent assistance tool that assists agents in their daily missions while ensuring data sovereignty, security, and compliance with regulatory requirements.
